{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Pishon.</b> It is the Nile, the river of Egypt. And because its waters spread and rise and water the land, it is called Pishon, as in ״וּפָשׁוּ פָרָשָׁיו״ (Habakkuk 1). Another interpretation: Pishon — because it grows flax, as is said of Egypt, ״וּבֹשׁוּ עֹבְדֵי פִשְׁתִּים״ (Isaiah 19)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:13.891609971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}